unting of those those rules  well I think there are two things I  think certainly we've seen some very  aggressive acts by some nations such as  Russia for example but I also think  we've seen the den agree  by Trump of some of those very  institutions that we rely on to keep  that peace and what did you make Donald  Trump's decision do you not visit the  war cemetery in France yesterday because  of the bad weather I was absolutely  horrified quite frankly when you think  of the sacrifice that people made and I  think people up and down the country and  across Europe whatever their political  views do think that it's very very  important that we commemorate what  happened and I think people were really  taken aback by that I think he made a  serious miss judge Monteux about the  mood across Europe I want to talk to you  about some comments that were made over  this week by a very prominent Labour  Party supporter about the poppy and  Aaron Bustani who is one of your most  high-profile activation who stays and  well he's very active on social media  said this I think the Poppy Appeal is  grotesque it has a kind of triumphalist  militarism about it it's racist right  it's right super white supremacists I  mean you're wearing a poppy well well  this is absolute nonsense and first of  all I must say this person no way  represents the name of party and I can  assure you that up and down the country  labour politicians will be proudly  wearing their puppy today they will be  at the Cenotaph this morning and they  recognize the huge sacrifice it has been  made by our armed forces both in the  first world war and in conflict since  and they recognized that this is a time  we come together and we remember and  that there has been so much good work  done by the Royal British Legion that I  finally know that the comments that that  this single person made completely I'm  representative and quite frankly an  utter disgrace I mean you say that's not  representative but here's so